{
  "id": "3ef2f8e6-c79f-47d5-876c-c91ac6f36462",
  "featureId": "cd083ad1-8310-4368-981b-d14c73c20d96",
  "number": 79,
  "shortId": "J5TXQ",
  "priority": 9,
  "slug": "gridui-08-drag-a-container-between-chrome-regions-dnd-hooks-the-plugin-escape-hatch",
  "title": "gridui-08: Drag a container between chrome regions — DnD hooks + the plugin escape hatch",
  "discussedAt": "",
  "contextReady": false,
  "contextReadyReason": "",
  "summary": "The drag framework ships but only the left sidebar is a drag surface. Regions and DockFrame have no hooks, so a container cannot be moved between regions.",
  "description": "Added 2026-07-26 after auditing docs/chrome-and-ui.md and docs/chrome-and-ui.md against\nthe planner. This was designed in both files (grid-ui plan §3, the old \"G6\") and tracked NOWHERE.\n\n═══ WHAT EXISTS ═══\nThe drag-and-drop framework SHIPPED and the app uses it: `heca-grid-ui/src/drag/` holds\n`context.rs`, `item.rs`, `math.rs`, `resolve.rs`, `state.rs`.\n- `DragSurfaceId` — a closed enum of drag surfaces.\n- `DragItem { surface, id: DragItemId, kind: DragItemKind, pane_id }`.\n- `SurfaceDragState { phase, hover_item, source_item, ghost_label }`, phase Idle → Starting → Dragging.\n- `DragContext { active_surface, surfaces }` — one mouse means one active surface, but EVERY\n  surface updates `hover_item`, so several drop targets can highlight at once. That is already the\n  cross-region model; nothing new is needed in the framework itself.\n- Dispatch and meaning are app-side (`heca/src/mouse/`), and every drop goes through the action\n  registry.\n\n═══ WHAT IS MISSING (verified in code 2026-07-26) ═══\n- `DragSurfaceId` has exactly ONE variant: `LeftSidebar`. Grep across heca/src and\n  heca-grid-ui/src finds no other. There is no right sidebar, no top/bottom bar, no region surface.\n- `DockFrame` (heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/dock_frame.rs) has NO drag handle. The widget was specified\n  with one (\"title bar + collapse toggle + drag handle + header-controls slot\") and it was never\n  built.\n- `ChromeRegion` sets no `hover_item`, so nothing can be dropped into it.\n⇒ A container cannot be moved from one region to another by any means. The plan calls this a\ncore capability of pluggable chrome (chrome plan §2.9: moving a container between regions is a\nhost concern).\n\n═══ WORK ═══\n1. Add region drag surfaces additively (right sidebar, top bar, bottom bar).\n2. Give `DockFrame` a drag handle that drives `SurfaceDragState` carrying a `DragItem`.\n3. Make `ChromeRegion` and the gaps between docks receive: set `hover_item` when they can accept.\n4. Render the ghost and the insertion line in the existing overlay layer.\n5. App side: on drop, DISPATCH AN ACTION (`chrome.dock.move_to_region`, `chrome.dock.reorder_before`)\n   through the registry. Never mutate directly.\n6. THE SAME MOVE MUST BE REACHABLE BY KEYBOARD AND RPC — grid-ui plan P2, and AGENTS.md's\n   input-parity rule. Drag is only the mouse surface for an action that must already exist. Build\n   the action first, then the drag on top of it.\n\n═══ THE PLUGIN ESCAPE HATCH (folded in from the same audit) ═══\n`DragSurfaceId` and `DragItemKind` are closed enums, so a plugin cannot add one at runtime. The\nagreed fix, recorded in grid-ui plan §3 and never tracked: ONE open variant each —\n`DragItemKind::Custom(u32)` so non-workspace containers do not inherit window-manager nouns, and\n`DragSurfaceId::Plugin(PluginSurfaceId)` funnelling dynamic surfaces through runtime dispatch while\nbuilt-ins keep the fast path. Not needed until plugins exist (F003/P001), but it belongs to this\nphase because it is the same code and the same decision.\n\n═══ THE RULE THAT MUST NOT BE BROKEN ═══\nExtend the framework ADDITIVELY. Add variants and files. NEVER modify or re-type an existing drag\ntype (keep `(f32,f32)` as-is, do not swap it for `Rectangle`) and NEVER remove or rename a variant.\nThe app constructs these types and matches on them exhaustively — adding a variant changes no\nbehaviour and the compiler simply asks for new match arms, which is the point of the closed enum.\n\n═══ VERIFICATION ═══\nDragging is visible, interactive behaviour. Green tests are not verification: build it and have the\nuser drag a container between two regions, and confirm the same move works from the keyboard.",
